  "basis": {
   "sampled": "Execution samples, allocation samples, lock and I/O events are charged to the innermost mod frame on their stack; game, JVM, loader and library frames above it count as that mod's work. Feature = how the game entered that mod (event bus \u2192 event handler, mixin handler name, or the block/entity/renderer/goal/screen class on the stack). Sampled values are estimates.",
   "perTick": "Share of server-thread samples \u00d7 mean measured tick duration. Interval is a binomial 95% range on that share; samples are autocorrelated, so treat it as approximate. Waits inside a tick are not sampled.",
   "perFrame": "Share of render-thread samples \u00d7 mean measured frame interval. GPU work, vsync and driver waits are not sampled, so this is CPU-side only.",
   "exact": "Timing probes measure every completed call of the selected method: exact call counts and wall time, including profiler overhead.",
   "heap": "Shallow bytes of live instances of each mod's own classes after a full GC at the end of the capture; objects of game or JDK classes that a mod holds are not included (not a retained-size analysis).",
   "threads": "Per-thread CPU load reported by the operating system through JFR (exact per interval, not sampled).",
   "mixins": "Mixin handlers merged into game classes are charged to the mod named in the handler (Fabric). Overwrites, unnamed handlers and @Unique helpers cannot be traced to a mod."
